  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sumatran Tiger protection and monitoring in Bukit Tigapuluh, Indonesia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Sumatran tiger is at the brink of extinction. Less than 500 individuals remain in the wild. Immediate on-site action and improved conservation planning are both needed to turn the fate of the Sumatran tiger around. Bukit Tigapuluh represents one of the last retreats of these tiders. The objectives of the project are, (1) To detect and deter poaching of tigers and tiger prey by implementing ranger foot patrols; (2) To support local police and forest police in their law enforcement efforts by providing key information on wildlife crime in the target area; (3) To monitor tigers in key areas by conducting camera trap surveys; (4) To support a collaborative, landscape-wide tiger survey by providing well-trained and experienced rangers and equipment for the field work; and, (5) To support the compilation of a site-specific tiger conservation action plan for Bukit Tigapuluh by assisting in survey data management and analysis.</narrative>
  </description>
